One day, Celestra fell deeply in love with a wandering musician whose songs made flowers bloom. They married beneath the dark sky, promising eternal devotion. But as fate would have it, a terrible plague swept through the village, claiming her beloved's life.

Heartbroken, Celestra climbed to the highest mountain, her loom strapped to her back. There, she wept for seven days and seven nights. Each tear that fell from her eyes transformed into a brilliant point of light as it rose into the heavens, suspended in the darkness.

When she could cry no more, Celestra began to weave. She worked her loom ceaselessly, threading together the lights her tears had created, forming patterns and pictures across the empty sky—a celestial tapestry in memory of her love.

The gods, moved by her devotion, immortalized her work. To this day, we see her tears shining as stars, connected by invisible threads, telling eternal stories across the night.

Write your own myth. Use your previous myth as inspiration, but adapt it in your own way.
Write 200 words. Format exactly:
Myth: [your story here].


